GITHUB ACTIONS CI/CD - COMPLETE IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE

OVERVIEW
========
GitHub Actions automates build, test and deployment.

FLOW
====
Code Change
   |
   v
Git Push
   |
   v
GitHub Repository
   |
   v
GitHub Actions
   |
   v
Build Docker Image
   |
   v
Deploy Server

STEP 1 - CREATE GITHUB REPOSITORY
=================================
Commands:
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial Commit"

Create repository on GitHub.

Add remote:
git remote add origin https://github.com/<user>/loan-ai-assistant.git

git push -u origin main

STEP 2 - CREATE WORKFLOW FOLDER
===============================
mkdir -p .github/workflows

Expected Structure:
.github/
└── workflows/

STEP 3 - CREATE WORKFLOW FILE
=============================
File Path:
.github/workflows/deploy.yml

Content:

name: Loan AI Pipeline

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout Repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Python
        uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: '3.11'

      - name: Install Dependencies
        run: |
          pip install -r requirements.txt

      - name: Validate Application
        run: |
          python -m py_compile app.py

STEP 4 - COMMIT WORKFLOW
========================
git add .
git commit -m "Add GitHub Actions"
git push

STEP 5 - VERIFY ACTIONS
=======================
Open GitHub Repository
Click Actions Tab

Expected:
Loan AI Pipeline

STEP 6 - ADD DOCKER BUILD
=========================
Add:

- name: Build Docker Image
  run: |
    docker build -t loan-ai .

STEP 7 - PREPARE DEPLOYMENT SERVER
==================================
Install Docker, Git and Docker Compose on Azure VM or AWS EC2.

STEP 8 - CREATE GITHUB SECRETS
==============================
Create:
SERVER_HOST
SERVER_USER
SERVER_SSH_KEY

STEP 9 - AUTO DEPLOYMENT
========================
Add SSH deployment step using appleboy/ssh-action.

STEP 10 - TEST CI/CD
====================
Make a code change and run:

git add .
git commit -m "test"
git push

Expected:
Pipeline starts automatically.

INTERVIEW ANSWER
================
I implemented CI/CD using GitHub Actions. Every push to the main branch validates the FastAPI application, builds a Docker image, and deploys the LangGraph-based AI assistant to a target server automatically.
